{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | sed -n '890,1230p'\"","aggregated_output":"   890\t<td>Nothing. The installed head stays.</td>\n   891\t<td><strong>Withholding is undetectable</strong>: silence and \"no new\n   892\thead\" look the same, and no timeout may tell them apart.</td></tr>\n   893\t<tr><td>A manifest nobody holds</td>\n   894\t<td><code>:yin.head/unloadable</code>; retried at the bounded delay;\n   895\tthe next observed trace replaces it at once.</td><td>-</td></tr>\n   896\t<tr><td>An older load never finishes</td>\n   897\t<td>Abandoned the moment a newer trace is observed; the newer one\n   898\tloads at once (5.5).</td><td>-</td></tr>\n   899\t<tr><td>A crash while installing</td>\n   900\t<td>Before the write: the previous head. After: the new one.</td>\n   901\t<td>-</td></tr>\n   902\t<tr><td><code>heads.edn</code> cannot be written</td>\n   903\t<td><code>:yin.head/unpersisted</code>; nothing installed; retried.</td>\n   904\t<td>No progress while the directory refuses writes.</td></tr>\n   905\t<tr><td>The publisher restarts, or the connection drops</td>\n   906\t<td><code>:source-lost</code>; a fresh handle; <code>:oldest</code>\n   907\tagain.</td><td>-</td></tr>\n   908\t<tr><td>The publisher's directory is lost, the key kept</td>\n   909\t<td>Traces from an empty directory are <code>:stale</code>.</td>\n   910\t<td>The publisher's remedy is 6.5's (5.2).</td></tr>\n   911\t<tr><td>The key is disclosed</td>\n   912\t<td>Whoever holds it moves the head. Remove the declaration.</td>\n   913\t<td>-</td></tr>\n   914\t</table>\n   915\t\n   916\t## 11. Implementation slices\n   917\t\n   918\tOrder: **H0 -> H1 -> H2 -> H3.** Each lands alone, green on the JVM,\n   919\tNode and Dart. H0 and H1 own disjoint source files.\n   920\t\n   921\t**H0 -- the trace and its rule.** Pure. Files: new\n   922\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc` (`trace`, `verify`, `seq-of`,\n   923\t`judge`), `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (the head prefix),\n   924\t`test/yin/vm/linker/sign_vectors.edn`, new\n   925\t`test/yin/vm/linker/head_test.cljc`. Complete when:\n   926\t- One trace under RFC 8032 TEST 1's seed is in the vectors with its\n   927\t  canonical bytes, signed message and signature, byte for byte on all\n   928\t  three hosts; one has a sequence above 2^32.\n   929\t- Tampering with the principal, manifest or sequence, a flipped\n   930\t  signature bit, another key, an extra key in either map, and a\n   931\t  name-envelope signature offered as a head proof each fail.\n   932\t- A trace through `dao.stream.cbor` verifies on each host.\n   933\t- **Sequence zero.** With a `nil` floor a trace of sequence 0 is a\n   934\t  candidate. With floor 0: sequence 1 a candidate, sequence 0 with the\n   935\t  installed manifest a duplicate, with another `:equivocation`. A\n   936\t  negative or non-integer sequence is `:malformed`. `seq-of` of one\n   937\t  transaction is 0, asserted against `dao.space.transactor`.\n   938\t- `judge` produces every row of 5.5, and its arity admits no source and\n   939\t  no candidate.\n   940\t- `seq-of` over a rehydrated index equals `seq-of` before the restart;\n   941\t  a further round raises it; two HEAD writes of one directory never\n   942\t  share it across rounds, name transactions, `(reset)` and the\n   943\t  unwritten-row recovery of `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 5.1. **If a HEAD\n   944\t  move that commits no transaction is found, the slice stops and 5.2 is\n   945\t  reopened.**\n   946\t\n   947\t**H1 -- the follower, over any reader.** No transport. Files:\n   948\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc` (`board`, `deposit!`, `follow`,\n   949\t`attach`, `step`, `install`, `heads`, `records`, `moved`),\n   950\t`src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc` (`abandon`; the kind-conflict refusal;\n   951\tthe wider client step), `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc` (`snapshots`\n   952\tadds installed heads), `src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc` (**refusal\n   953\ttranslation for the two host load operations**),\n   954\t`test/dao/space/dht_test.cljc`, `test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc`, new\n   955\t`test/yin/vm/linker/head_follow_test.cljc`. Amendments carried:\n   956\t`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 1, 7.2, 9, 10 and 13 (D2; `abandon`; the\n   957\trefusal and its failure-vocabulary row); `dao.jing.dht.md` section 1 (a\n   958\tpointer here). In every case the reader is handed the publisher's board\n   959\tring directly as its reader handle, and blobs travel over the mesh\n   960\tseam. Complete when:\n   961\t- **Existing tests.** `forget` is untouched, and\n   962\t  `forget-clears-a-terminal-record-and-is-refused-while-loading` passes\n   963\t  as written. Any existing test that loads one address under two kinds\n   964\t  and relies on the silent no-op is migrated, and the slice names it.\n   965\t- **The host module translates the refusal.** `dht-answer`\n   966\t  (`yin/repl/query.cljc:665-674`) calls `load-index` and `load-module`\n   967\t  bare today; only the publication operations catch a\n   968\t  `:dao.space.dht/refused` (`625-633`). Both load operations now answer\n   969\t  a refusal as the call's error value, under its own code, and the\n   970\t  interpreter never throws. Tested through the host module: a\n   971\t  `(dao.space.dht/load-index m)` while `m` loads as a candidate, and a\n   972\t  `load-module` of an address recorded under another kind, each answer\n   973\t  `:dao.space.dht/kind-conflict` as data, the serve round continues,\n   974\t  and the next request is answered.\n   975\t- **`abandon` and the fetch client.** `abandon` removes a `:loading`\n   976\t  record, emits no event, and is refused for a record that is not\n   977\t  loading. Four cases, each on the last and only load, each asserting\n   978\t  afterwards that the client holds no unsent request, no outstanding id\n   979\t  and no completion, **with no load active**:\n   980\t  - abandoned before submission, the request ring full, so the request\n   981\t    was retained unsent;\n   982\t  - abandoned after submission, the answer not yet arrived;\n   983\t  - the same, then the late answer arrives: it is dropped, no blob is\n   984\t    stored through it, and no event is produced;\n   985\t  - the same address loaded again afterwards: it gets a new request id\n   986\t    and completes on its own answer.\n   987\t  A fifth: two loads fetching one address, one abandoned; the other\n   988\t  completes.\n   989\t- **Shared candidates.** Principals P and Q whose current traces name\n   990\t  one manifest: one record, both owners. P's candidate is replaced\n   991\t  while it loads: the record is still loading and Q's head is then\n   992\t  installed from it. P's trace is rejected `:seq-mismatch` while Q's is\n   993\t  right: Q installs; the record is removed only at the second release.\n   994\t  After both are installed the record is gone, and a `load-index` of\n   995\t  that manifest by hand is `:loaded` with zero `:jing/get`.\n   996\t- A publishes `alib` and deposits; B, given the board and A's principal\n   997\t  and no manifest, installs A's head and resolves `alib`. A republishes;\n   998\t  B resolves the new address.\n   999\t- **First transaction.** A first index deposits sequence 0; a\n  1000\t  first-contact reader installs it; sequence 1 replaces it.\n  1001\t- Ten deposits between two polls install one head, the last.\n  1002\t- **A candidate is not resolvable.** While the candidate is `:loaded`\n  1003\t  and not installed, and between `:confirmed` and `install`,\n  1004\t  `snapshots` does not list it and a name asserted only in it is\n  1005\t  `:absent`.\n  1006\t- **A wrong-sequence trace X** (sequence 1000000 over an index at 10,\n  1007\t  holding a newer assertion of `alib`), from floor 10 and from a `nil`\n  1008\t  floor, with true heads 11 and 12, in each order: X, 11, 12; 11, X, 12;\n  1009\t  11, 12, X; X while 11 is loading. Each run ends with the last true\n  1010\t  head shown installed, the floor equal to its sequence, `alib` never\n  1011\t  resolved through X, and X not loaded a second time when shown again.\n  1012\t- **An unfinished load does not block.** The mesh never answers for a\n  1013\t  blob of head 11, so its load stays `:loading` for the whole test.\n  1014\t  Head 12, whose blobs are all local to the mesh, is deposited: 12 is\n  1015\t  installed, 11's record is gone in the step 12 was observed, and no\n  1016\t  tick count is asserted to have ended 11.\n  1017\t- **Alternating replay, the stated limit.** From floor 10 the source\n  1018\t  alternates signed 11 and 13 at every poll, and the mesh answers no\n  1019\t  fetch within a turn: nothing is installed while it lasts, the floor\n  1020\t  stays 10, loading records never exceed one, and the client holds\n  1021\t  nothing between turns. The same alternation with fetches answered:\n  1022\t  11 installs, then 13, and 11 is `:stale` from then on. Two\n  1023\t  wrong-sequence traces alternating are each walked each turn with zero\n  1024\t  `:jing/get` after the first, and neither is ever resolvable.\n  1025\t- **An unloadable candidate** keeps the previous head, is started again\n  1026\t  only after the delay, and is replaced at once by the next trace.\n  1027\t- **A failed load made by hand.** The test calls `load-index` on a\n  1028\t  manifest no peer holds; it fails. The publisher's head names that\n  1029\t  manifest and the blobs then appear. The follower restarts the load as\n  1030\t  an index load after the delay; it loads; the head is installed; the\n  1031\t  record is still of the index kind and still listed by\n  1032\t  `loaded-indexes`. A `load-index` by hand while a candidate of that\n  1033\t  address is loading is `:dao.space.dht/kind-conflict`.\n  1034\t- **Durable before used.** After `:confirmed` and before `install`: the\n  1035\t  floor, the snapshot set and `heads` under `:installed` are unchanged.\n  1036\t  A follower composed again from the old records is at the old head. One\n  1037\t  composed again from the new records, `install` never called, is at\n  1038\t  the new head with zero `:jing/get` on the request ring, and refuses\n  1039\t  the older trace as `:stale`. `install` of any other trace is refused.\n  1040\t- **A lost source.** A reader handle answering `cursor-mismatch`, and\n  1041\t  one answering `end`, each produce `:source-lost` once; after `attach`\n  1042\t  of a fresh handle the current head is read again and judged a\n  1043\t  duplicate.\n  1044\t- `deposit!` refuses `:seq-collision`, `:seq-regression`, `:empty` and\n  1045\t  `:no-key`, each appending nothing.\n  1046\t- Two nodes following each other reach quiescence; neither HEAD moves.\n  1047\t- `moved` names exactly the linked names whose address changed.\n  1048\t\n  1049\t**H2 -- name resolution, and the board over WebSocket on loopback.**\n  1050\tFiles: `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc` (the named `descriptor`\n  1051\trequest in the mirror; the link's `resolve`),\n  1052\t`src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc` (a name map on the acceptor and\n  1053\tthe dial; `resolve` on a dial before any reflection),\n  1054\t`test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc`, new\n  1055\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc`, new\n  1056\t`test/yin/vm/linker/head_ws_test.cljc`. Amendments carried, all in\n  1057\t`dao.stream.remote.md`: section 2, the name map as composition data\n  1058\tbeside the table; 2.1, the named request shape, and `not-found`\n  1059\tcarrying the name; 2.3, a step 0 that resolves a name or answers\n  1060\t`not-found`, and a named request with another op as malformed; 2.4, the\n  1061\tlink's `resolve`; section 5, the head board as a convention and the\n  1062\tsentence that a name is lookup data and never a `:dao.stream/identity`;\n  1063\tand its status line, which says \"design target\" of code that exists\n  1064\t(so does `dao.stream.ws.md`'s). **`dao.stream.md` is not amended.** If\n  1065\tthis slice's review finds it must be, the slice stops and that becomes\n  1066\tan owner question; no fallback is designed, because none is expected.\n  1067\tComplete when:\n  1068\t- **Resolution.** A mirror with a name map answers a named `descriptor`\n  1069\t  with the entry's own identity and surface; an unmapped name, and a\n  1070\t  name mapped to an identity the table lacks, are `not-found` with the\n  1071\t  name; a named `next` is dropped. `resolve` answers retry, then `ok`\n  1072\t  with a remote descriptor that `attach!` accepts. Every existing\n  1073\t  `dao.stream.remote` test passes unchanged: an identity request is\n  1074\t  answered as before.\n  1075\t- **Identity.** The reader's reflection reports the ring's own\n  1076\t  identity, never the name. No value on the wire carries the name under\n  1077\t  `:dao.stream/identity`.\n  1078\t- A serving node and a dialing node on loopback: the reader's handle is\n  1079\t  a reflection; H1's first case passes over it unchanged.\n  1080\t- **Restart.** The publisher's endpoint is stopped and started: the\n  1081\t  reader reports `:source-lost`, dials and resolves again, receives a\n  1082\t  different identity, and reads the head, judged a duplicate. A cursor\n  1083\t  kept from the old ring is `cursor-mismatch` on the new one.\n  1084\t- **A shared key.** Two serving nodes with one key answer two\n  1085\t  identities for the one name; a reader of each reads its own ring.\n  1086\t- The table holds the board and nothing else; a writer op on it is\n  1087\t  `no-surface`; another identity is `not-found`.\n  1088\t- A bind host that is not a loopback literal composes no endpoint, for\n  1089\t  IPv4 and IPv6 literals.\n  1090\t- A TCP port already in use is a refusal as data, and the node keeps\n  1091\t  running without a board.\n  1092\t- The same cases pass on Node and on Dart.\n  1093\t\n  1094\t**H3 -- the REPL.** Files: `src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc`,\n  1095\t`src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc`,\n  1096\t`src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc` (the `yin.head` host module),\n  1097\t`src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` (the\n  1098\tfirst-contact pending), `test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj`, the tests\n  1099\tbeside each, and the `yin.repl` documents. Complete when:\n  1100\t- The token prints once, as `yin:<host:port>/<principal>`, only when\n  1101\t  the board endpoint is bound; `parse-token` refuses a third part with\n  1102\t  the pin message.\n  1103\t- `dht join <token>` passes no `--dht-manifest` and saves\n  1104\t  `--dht-follow`; a bare restart resolves from `heads.edn` before any\n  1105\t  connection is made.\n  1106\t- `--dht-follow` of an undeclared principal refuses startup.\n  1107\t  `--dht-manifest` with a saved follow suspends following for that run.\n  1108\t- A `(require 'alib)` typed before the first head parks, and completes\n  1109\t  on the install with no typed line; `(abandon)` ends it.\n  1110\t- **The write precedes the install.** A seam that fails the write\n  1111\t  prints `:yin.head/unpersisted`, installs nothing, and installs after\n  1112\t  the retry. A process killed between write and install restarts at the\n  1113\t  new head; one killed before the write restarts at the old.\n  1114\t- An installed head that moves a linked name prints the line of 5.7;\n  1115\t  the repeat require is unchanged; `(reset)` then `require` links the\n  1116\t  new address.\n  1117\t- `heads.edn` cases: absent, malformed, a record that fails\n  1118\t  verification, a record for an unfollowed principal; each read on Dart.\n  1119\t- **End to end, both processes on loopback.** A publishes `alib`; B\n  1120\t  joins with the token and requires it on each of the four VMs, on the\n  1121\t  JVM and on Node. A republishes; B, after `(reset)`, links the new\n  1122\t  module. B restarted with A stopped still requires it.\n  1123\t- The host module holds no rule: no fold, verification or file write in\n  1124\t  `yin.repl.query`.\n  1125\t\n  1126\t## 12. Deferred\n  1127\t\n  1128\tEach of the first four is its own later design; section 8.2 says what\n  1129\tit adds and amends.\n  1130\t\n  1131\t- **Serving off loopback**, over WebSocket (8.3). First after the core.\n  1132\t- **Relaying.** Decided as a deferral: no node re-serves a head in the\n  1133\t  core.\n  1134\t- **Many sources per principal.**\n  1135\t- **UDP on the DHT socket, with a return-path proof**, fragments\n  1136\t  included.\n  1137\t- **`wss`**, and with it a narrower first-contact limit and no path\n  1138\t  attacker to churn the candidate.\n  1139\t- **A progress guarantee under replay**: a reviewed scheduling policy\n  1140\t  for the candidate. Not promised by the core (5.5).\n  1141\t- **The `yin.repl` service's fixed identities** (C4). A landed defect\n  1142\t  against `dao.stream.md`, outside this design. Its fix is to resolve\n  1143\t  `yin.repl/requests` and `yin.repl/answers` as names, with H2's\n  1144\t  mechanism. Named here so it is not lost; it needs its own task.\n  1145\t- **Finding sources** beyond the address given (rendezvous).\n  1146\t- **Liveness** by a `dao.lease` composition over the last-answer reading.\n  1147\t- **Relink in place.**\n  1148\t- **Resolving a transitive require by its pinned address**\n  1149\t  (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` section 13); following makes its absence felt.\n  1150\t- **Collecting superseded indexes; key rotation; a head history; a\n  1151\t  durable last-rejected; a browser follower; push.**\n  1152\t\n  1153\t## 13. Questions only the owner can answer\n  1154\t\n  1155\t1. **Does \"always\" reach into a live session?** The design keeps a\n  1156\t   session on the module it linked, reports the move, and links the new\n  1157\t   one after `(reset)`. If a repeat `(require 'alib)` must switch a\n  1158\t   running session, relink in place needs its own design first. No\n  1159\t   ruling settles this.\n  1160\t2. **What should a bare `q` see after `dht join`?** Already ruled: the\n  1161\t   publisher's facts are a separate db-value and union is explicit.\n  1162\t   Open: the default. Today join hydrates, so a bare `q` answers the\n  1163\t   publisher's facts. Here join does not, so it answers the reader's own\n  1164\t   index, and the publisher's is `(dao.space.dht/q <manifest> ...)` with\n  1165\t   the manifest from `(yin.head/heads)`. Choose: (a) that; (b) a bare\n  1166\t   `q` unions the installed heads by default; (c) a named view.\n  1167\t   Recommendation: (a) now, (c) on request.\n  1168\t3. **Is every HEAD move the head you mean?** A follower loads a new\n  1169\t   index for each round the publisher evaluates, not only for each\n  1170\t   `yin.link/publish`. \"Whatever the HEAD is\" reads that way and the\n  1171\t   design follows it; it was said before this cost was stated. The\n  1172\t   alternative, a head only at each publish, is quieter and leaves a\n  1173\t   follower's view of the publisher's facts behind its names.\n  1174\t   Recommendation: every HEAD move.\n  1175\t4. **Is WebSocket acceptable as the first cross-machine transport?** It\n  1176\t   needs one side to accept a TCP connection, at the same port number\n  1177\t   as its UDP socket, and it does not hole-punch: two peers both behind\n  1178\t   NATs would need a relay pair, or the deferred UDP design. It is\n  1179\t   cleartext until `wss`. It is also the step that needs no new proof\n  1180\t   (8.3). Recommendation: yes.\n  1181\t5. **Is safety without a progress guarantee acceptable for the core?**\n  1182\t   The core never installs a wrong or older head. It does not promise a\n  1183\t   newer one is ever installed: a source can withhold, and on a\n  1184\t   cleartext channel a path attacker can alternate old signed heads so\n  1185\t   that no load completes (5.5). On loopback the attacker is someone\n  1186\t   already on the machine. Off loopback it is anyone on the path, so\n  1187\t   this question is really about question 4's step: either accept that\n  1188\t   limit there, or require `wss` or a scheduling policy first.\n  1189\t   Recommendation: accept it for the core; decide again at the step\n  1190\t   off loopback.\n  1191\t\n  1192\t**None of the five blocks adoption of the core.** Questions 1 to 3\n  1193\tchoose behaviour the slices can change late (a notice, a default view,\n  1194\twhen `deposit!` is called). Questions 4 and 5 gate the step after the\n  1195\tcore, not the core.\n  1196\t\n  1197\t**One named blocker that is not the owner's.** Slice H2 amends\n  1198\t`dao.stream.remote.md`, a contract whose every sentence is a rule, with\n  1199\tthe name map and the named `descriptor` request. That amendment needs\n  1200\tthe Architect's and the independent reviewer's sign-off on the contract\n  1201\ttext itself before H2 lands. H0 and H1 do not depend on it.\n  1202\t\n  1203\tNo longer questions: whether a node relays by default, and the order of\n  1204\tthe return-path proof, are deferred with their designs; publisher\n  1205\trecovery needs no decision, since its remedy is untouched; the board's\n  1206\tidentity is decided (C3) without amending the identity contract.\n  1207\t\n  1208\t## Revision 1 (2026-10-05), in brief\n  1209\t\n  1210\tThe first review's eight findings were all accepted. What survives of\n  1211\tthat revision here: the `nil` floor and sequence 0; a snapshot set that\n  1212\tnever holds a candidate; a floor of confirmed evidence only; confirm,\n  1213\tpersist, install; loopback-only serving; `deposit!` taking datoms; the\n  1214\tpublisher's recovery remedy kept. What it added and this revision\n  1215\tremoves: load holders, a candidate set, the named `descriptor` request,\n  1216\trelay rings, `--dht-recover`, the removal of hydration, and slice H5.\n  1217\t\n  1218\t## Revision 2 (2026-10-05)\n  1219\t\n  1220\tThe owner chose the simple core and asked whether cross-machine use\n  1221\twould then need a redesign. The document was rewritten, not patched,\n  1222\tand section 8 is the answer. The second review's five findings\n  1223\t(<code>collab/1791205158504-reviewer-architect-head-trace-r2.gpt-6.1-sol<!--\n  1224\t-->.findings.md</code>):\n  1225\t\n  1226\t1. **Candidate eviction starvation (P1): eliminated.** There is one\n  1227\t   candidate slot and no eviction. The latest observed trace takes it,\n  1228\t   even over a higher claimed sequence, so four unloadable high traces\n  1229\t   cannot shut out a true head (5.5).\n  1230\t2. **An unfinished load blocking newer heads (P1): still applicable,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
