{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '876,921p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '440,480p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '354,387p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | sed -n '1245,1328p'; rg -n 'sign-off|resolve|name' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | tail -14\"","aggregated_output":"   876\t(defn- read-facts\n   877\t  \"Apply every fact the DHT appended.  A lost fact reports every live\n   878\t   publication unknown, never acknowledged, and ends it.\"\n   879\t  [node]\n   880\t  (let [[facts cursor gap?] (read-all (get-in node [:composition :facts])\n   881\t                                      (:facts node))\n   882\t        wanted (fetching node)\n   883\t        node (reduce #(apply-fact %1 %2 wanted) (assoc node :facts cursor)\n   884\t                     facts)]\n   885\t    (if gap?\n   886\t      [(assoc node :pubs [] :fresh [] :repair [] :queued {} :repair-owner {}\n   887\t              :inflight {})\n   888\t       (mapv #(hash-map ::event :publication-unknown :manifest (:manifest %))\n   889\t             (:pubs node))]\n   890\t      [node []])))\n   891\t\n   892\t\n   893\t;; =============================================================================\n   894\t;; Reports (5.5.3): the first report, every change, and the ends\n   895\t;; =============================================================================\n   896\t\n   897\t(defn- report\n   898\t  [kind pub]\n   899\t  (let [r (result pub)\n   900\t        failed (->> (:order pub)\n   901\t                    (keep (fn [a]\n   902\t                            (let [e (get-in pub [:entries a])]\n   903\t                              (when-not (= :sent (:state e))\n   904\t                                (cond-> {:address a :reason (:reason e)\n   905\t                                         :peers (or (:peers e) 0)}\n   906\t                                  (:was e) (assoc :was (:was e)))))))\n   907\t                    (sort-by (comp str :address))\n   908\t                    vec)]\n   909\t    (cond-> {::event kind\n   910\t             :manifest (:manifest pub)\n   911\t             :result r\n   912\t             :blobs (:blobs pub)\n   913\t             :sent (:sent pub)\n   914\t             :failed failed\n   915\t             :repairing? (and (not= :acknowledged r) (nil? (:ended pub)))}\n   916\t      (pos? (:sent pub)) (assoc :peers (:min-peers pub))\n   917\t      (:ended pub) (assoc :ended (:ended pub)))))\n   918\t\n   919\t\n   920\t(defn- close-cycle\n   921\t  [node pub]\n   440\t\n   441\t      (unacknowledged-answer? answer)\n   442\t      (finish {:error (unacknowledged answer)})\n   443\t\n   444\t      :else\n   445\t      (let [verdict (and (put-answer? answer)\n   446\t                         (get answer :jing/result))]\n   447\t        (cond\n   448\t          (= :inserted verdict) (finish {:result :inserted})\n   449\t          (= :present verdict)\n   450\t          [published\n   451\t           (assoc records (get record :put-id)\n   452\t                  (assoc record :phase :verify-unissued))\n   453\t           (dissoc routes id)]\n   454\t          :else (finish {:error malformed-response}))))))\n   455\t\n   456\t\n   457\t(defn- route-completions\n   458\t  \"Order 5's routing: fold the drained completions against the live\n   459\t   records, then return the published entries and the successor records\n   460\t   and routes.\"\n   461\t  [completions records routes]\n   462\t  (let [[published records routes]\n   463\t        (reduce (fn [[published records routes] completion]\n   464\t                  (if-some [put-id (get routes (:id completion))]\n   465\t                    (if-some [record (get records put-id)]\n   466\t                      (materialize-on-completion\n   467\t                        completion record published records routes)\n   468\t                      [(conj published (decode-plain-completion completion))\n   469\t                       records\n   470\t                       routes])\n   471\t                    [(conj published (decode-plain-completion completion))\n   472\t                     records\n   473\t                     routes]))\n   474\t                [[] records routes]\n   475\t                completions)]\n   476\t    {:published published :records records :routes routes}))\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\t;; =============================================================================\n   480\t;; Orders 2 to 4 -- the polls and the verify reads\n   354\t   :jing/unacknowledged reason}.\"\n   355\t  [v]\n   356\t  (and (map? v)\n   357\t       (= #{:jing/request :jing/unacknowledged} (set (keys v)))))\n   358\t\n   359\t\n   360\t(defn- unacknowledged\n   361\t  \"The error map an unacknowledged write answer completes with.\"\n   362\t  [answer]\n   363\t  {:code unacknowledged-code\n   364\t   :reason (get answer :jing/unacknowledged)})\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn- decode-plain-completion\n   368\t  \"Total decode of one completion no materialization claims: the answer\n   369\t   conforms to its request's vocabulary or the completion carries an\n   370\t   :error; a loss carries :lost.\"\n   371\t  [completion]\n   372\t  (let [{:keys [id request lost answer]} completion]\n   373\t    (cond\n   374\t      lost {:id id, :lost lost}\n   375\t\n   376\t      (contains? request get-op)\n   377\t      (cond\n   378\t        (not (get-answer? answer)) {:id id, :error malformed-response}\n   379\t        (not (get answer :jing/found?))\n   380\t        {:id id, :found? false, :value nil}\n   381\t        :else\n   382\t        (let [value (accepted-value (get request get-op)\n   383\t                                    (get answer :jing/bytes))]\n   384\t          (if (identical? refused value)\n   385\t            {:id id, :error integrity-failure}\n   386\t            {:id id, :found? true, :value value})))\n   387\t\n  1245\t   8.2 makes pre-reassembly proof on the outer fragment envelope a\n  1246\t   stated requirement of that later design, with `dao.stream.udp` and\n  1247\t   `dao.stream.remote.md` in its scope.\n  1248\t\n  1249\tThe first review's finding 4, left \"partly\" resolved: re-checked against\n  1250\tthe one-slot rule and resolved. A wrong or unloadable signed trace can\n  1251\toccupy the slot only while it is the newest thing the source shows; the\n  1252\tnext trace replaces it, and the floor never moved. A source that keeps\n  1253\tshowing it is withholding, which no rule can beat (section 10).\n  1254\t\n  1255\tFound while rewriting:\n  1256\t\n  1257\t- **N5. The tree already uses well-known names as mirror-table\n  1258\t  identities** (`yin.repl/requests`, `yin.repl/answers`). The first\n  1259\t  review's finding 3 was argued from the contract alone; the landed\n  1260\t  REPL service has the same shape. Revision 2 followed that shape for\n  1261\t  the board; revision 3 withdraws that (C3, C4).\n  1262\t- **N6. The REPL's `--port` endpoint cannot carry the board.** Its table\n  1263\t  holds the evaluation service; exposing the head there would expose\n  1264\t  evaluation with it. The board has its own endpoint (5.1).\n  1265\t- **N7. `dao.space.dht/load` is silent across kinds** (D3).\n  1266\t- **N8. Revision 1 removed hydration to fix D1 and then had to add\n  1267\t  `--dht-recover` to restore what that broke.** The defect was only\n  1268\t  that join used it. Revision 2 stops join using it and touches nothing\n  1269\t  else (5.8).\n  1270\t\n  1271\t## Revision 3 (2026-10-05)\n  1272\t\n  1273\tThe third review\n  1274\t(<code>collab/1791207836775-reviewer-architect-head-trace-r3.gpt-6.1-sol<!--\n  1275\t-->.findings.md</code>)\n  1276\tfound five new defects. Each citation was checked; all five are\n  1277\taccepted.\n  1278\t\n  1279\t1. **The board name as an identity (P1, accepted).** Choice (a): a name\n  1280\t   is lookup data, resolved to the ring's real descriptor by a named\n  1281\t   `descriptor` request, and the reader then attaches normally.\n  1282\t   `dao.stream.md` is untouched, so no owner decision is needed. Choice\n  1283\t   (b), a name as a legal identity, would amend the governing contract\n  1284\t   and need cursor semantics for a stream replaced under its name.\n  1285\t   Choice (c), an endpoint whose address is the identity, does not\n  1286\t   exist: the address is not the ring's identity, and any fixed entry\n  1287\t   key is the alias again. Revision 2's note N5 read the landed\n  1288\t   `yin.repl` aliases as a convention to follow; they are a defect\n  1289\t   (C4). Its claim that the question blocked only relaying is withdrawn\n  1290\t   (8.2). Changed: C3, C4, 5.1, section 6, 8.2, 8.3, section 9, H2,\n  1291\t   section 12.\n  1292\t2. **Shared candidate ownership (P1, accepted).** The follower keeps an\n  1293\t   owner set per candidate record and removes the record only at the\n  1294\t   last release; release happens at replacement, rejection and\n  1295\t   installation. Changed: 5.5, H1.\n  1296\t3. **Host refusal translation (P1, accepted).** Both host load\n  1297\t   operations answer a DHT refusal as data; in H1 with a test through\n  1298\t   the host module. Changed: 5.5, H1.\n  1299\t4. **Abandon and the fetch client (P2, accepted).** `abandon` retires\n  1300\t   the record's client interest with two functions that exist\n  1301\t   (`content.step/abandon`, `retire`), and the client is stepped\n  1302\t   whenever it holds anything, not only while a load is active.\n  1303\t   Changed: 5.5, section 6, H1. This also finishes the second review's\n  1304\t   partly resolved items: its #2 by this and by item 2, its #3 by\n  1305\t   item 2.\n  1306\t5. **Replay and load frequency overstated (P2, accepted).** The core\n  1307\t   states that it gives safety and no progress guarantee, bounds the\n  1308\t   work an alternation can cause, and withdraws \"loaded once per\n  1309\t   process\". Changed: 5.5, 5.9, 8.4, section 10, H1, section 12,\n  1310\t   question 5.\n  1311\t\n  1312\tSmall corrections applied: the mirror-call citation now runs to line\n  1313\t276, and 8.2 says what the reserved `ws:<port>` does not cover.\n  1314\t\n  1315\tFound while revising: **N9.** `dht-answer` lets any refusal thrown by\n  1316\t`load-index` or `load-module` through the host interpreter today, not\n  1317\tonly the new one; H1's translation covers every\n  1318\t`:dao.space.dht/refused` code on both operations.\n  1319\t\n  1320\t## Lineage\n  1321\t\n  1322\tThe tuple space made stigmergy precise; this makes one trace of it\n  1323\tdurable enough to follow. `announce!` was already the deposit, kept\n  1324\tprivate. A head board is the same act with an author and an audience: a\n  1325\tsigned value on a ring one agent writes and any agent may read, carried\n  1326\tby whatever carries a stream. Datomic's connection hands a peer the\n  1327\tnewest database value; here no connection is the abstraction, only the\n  1328\ttrace, and each reader decides whose traces are worth following.\n1173:   follower's view of the publisher's facts behind its names.\n1197:**One named blocker that is not the owner's.** Slice H2 amends\n1199:the name map and the named `descriptor` request. That amendment needs\n1200:the Architect's and the independent reviewer's sign-off on the contract\n1215:removes: load holders, a candidate set, the named `descriptor` request,\n1242:   H1 names any test the kind-conflict refusal migrates.\n1249:The first review's finding 4, left \"partly\" resolved: re-checked against\n1250:the one-slot rule and resolved. A wrong or unloadable signed trace can\n1257:- **N5. The tree already uses well-known names as mirror-table\n1279:1. **The board name as an identity (P1, accepted).** Choice (a): a name\n1280:   is lookup data, resolved to the ring's real d